course: dictionary
lesson: 9991
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word tee is a good example. The words around it show you which meaning is right, so read the context before you decide.
explain: In golf, a tee is a small peg that holds the ball up before you hit it. The tee is also the flat place where each hole begins. In tee-ball, young children hit a ball from a stand called a tee.
explain: In everyday talk, tee is short for T-shirt, as in the French «des tee-shirts roses» (pink T-shirts). Tee can also be the letter T: the letters C-A-T are said «see-ay-tee».
fact: A tee is a small peg that holds a golf ball up before it is hit.
fact: To tee off is to make the first hit in golf. To tee up is to put the ball on a tee, or to get something ready.
fact: Informally, tee means T-shirt, so «des tee-shirts roses» means pink T-shirts.
fact: «Fits to a T» or «to a tee» means exactly or perfectly.
fact: «Teed off» is US slang that means annoyed.
exercise: In golf, what is a tee? | A rainy day on the course | A club for hitting the ball far | *A small peg that holds the ball up before it is hit | A flag on the green
exercise: «des tee-shirts roses» means pink T-shirts. What does tee mean here? | A golf peg | The first hit in golf | A letter in a word | *A T-shirt
exercise: Mia says, «My new hat fits to a T.» What does she mean? | *It fits perfectly | It is made of cotton | It is a hat for golf only | It is too big and falls off
test: Which phrase means to make the first hit in golf? | Tee up | Tee-ball | Fits to a T | *Tee off
test: Ravi says, «Dad teed off when the bus was late.» What does teed off mean? | Dad was happy and laughing | *Dad was annoyed | Dad was playing golf | Dad was lost
exam: In the sentence «see-ay-tee» spells the word cat, what does tee stand for? | A tee shirt | *The letter T | A flat place where a golf hole begins | A golf peg
